---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://qrcode.page/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Guides', item: 'https://qrcode.page/guides' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Restaurant QR Menus', item: 'https://qrcode.page/guides/how-to-use-qr-codes-for-restaurants' },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to Use QR Codes for Contactless Restaurant Menus"
  description="A complete hospitality guide on creating contactless QR menus, tabletop display recommendations, dynamic price updates, and Google review collection."
  canonical="https://qrcode.page/guides/how-to-use-qr-codes-for-restaurants"
  jsonLd={breadcrumbJsonLd}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-16 space-y-8">
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-400" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-indigo-600">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/guides" class="hover:text-indigo-600">Guides</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 truncate">Restaurant QR Menus</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="space-y-3">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight leading-tight">
        How to Use QR Codes for Contactless Restaurant Menus
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">Updated August 2026 • 6 min read</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-6 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
      <p>
        Digital QR menus have revolutionized the restaurant industry by eliminating expensive reprinting cycles, enabling instant seasonal price updates, and providing hygienic touchless dining.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-2">1. Always Use Dynamic QR Codes</h2>
      <p>
        Never print a static PDF URL on tabletop acrylic stands. If your menu prices change or you introduce new chef specials, a <strong>Dynamic QR code</strong> allows you to update your digital menu instantly in your dashboard without reprinting a single physical tabletop sticker.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-2">2. Optimize for Fast Mobile Loading</h2>
      <p>
        Guests in restaurants often browse on cellular data. Avoid massive 50MB PDF downloads. Our hosted <strong>QR Restaurant Menu</strong> generates ultra-lightweight, mobile-first web menus with categorized starters, mains, drinks, and dietary labels that load in under a second.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-2">3. Combine Menus with Guest Wi-Fi &amp; Google Reviews</h2>
      <p>
        Maximize table engagement by placing a dual-action card: a <strong>Menu QR</strong> on the front and a <strong>Google Review QR</strong> or <strong>Wi-Fi QR</strong> on the back.
      </p>

      <div class="pt-4">
        <a href="/restaurant-menu-qr-code" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-2xl font-bold text-xs bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 text-white shadow-md">
          Create Restaurant Menu QR &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
